  Dataset:a dataset is a structured collection of data used for analysis, modeling, and decision-making. It is the raw material that data scientists work with to uncover patterns, build insights, and train machine learning models.
Forward fill:Forward fill takes the previous available value and copies it down to fill the missing value.
Backward fill:Backward fill takes the next available value and fills the missing value with it.
Linear interpolation:Linear interpolation is a method of estimating a missing value by connecting the known values with a straight line.

